                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aec1e08a-dbad-3153-9597-a3abfe5fc232",
                                        "entry_id": "a1c95588-9199-30b6-b12a-120ac6715385",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The set of all the vertices adjacent to a given vertex."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "US",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2a4342f8-9302-33ff-927e-6d20ff493682",
                                        "entry_id": "a1c95588-9199-30b6-b12a-120ac6715385",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The set of all the vertices adjacent to a given vertex.",
                                            "The set of all cells near a given cell used to determine that cell's state in the next generation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "US",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1bebd2ac-fd3a-4019-9ca3-348fca69d012",
                                                "sense_id": "2a4342f8-9302-33ff-927e-6d20ff493682",
                                                "text": "In fact, it looks at the number of states and the neighborhood of the rule (determined by the filename), and decides whether to make it a lookup-table, or a \"computed-function\" rule."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f993e3a8-a7d8-496b-8a35-7951a612d946",
                                                "sense_id": "2a4342f8-9302-33ff-927e-6d20ff493682",
                                                "text": "Universal: Is able to simulate other CA, the neighborhood size may be limited but the number of cell value should be unlimited (big neighborhoods can be transformed into multivalued cells)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d87c5a0-d394-4218-8c60-114e07de8838",
                                                "sense_id": "2a4342f8-9302-33ff-927e-6d20ff493682",
                                                "text": "I've seen this space colloqually referred to as MAP (presumably since it maps a 3x3 neighborhood into a future cell state), or more precisely and if you want to be pedantic, since there are a lot of variants of cellular automata: 2D Range-1 Moore neighborhood 2-state (non-totalistic) cellular automata (regular euclidean grid implied, although some people explore toroidal configurations, nonstandard tilings, or arbitrary graphs)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "af08a577-b549-492e-b348-8d954007994b",
                        "source_entry_id": "70b54f9b-6078-3d80-9a74-5768f43d27ba",
                        "source_sense_id": "967a98fb-7a1a-3791-95b2-2fa57b7e22a3",
                        "source_sense_description": "Gegend, die hauptsächlich zum Wohnen genutzt wird, also nicht gewerblich oder industriell",
                        "target_lang_word": "neighbourhood",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "neighbourhood",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "acb5668c-1d1d-3b1b-9284-332537f9454b",
                                        "entry_id": "e2357106-d76c-35f3-b6dd-55d898a80e72",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "British standard spelling of neighborhood."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1283b55a-5964-4bbb-8cfc-6f259d22f2ca",
                                                "sense_id": "acb5668c-1d1d-3b1b-9284-332537f9454b",
                                                "text": "These developments, most of which have taken place during the past 30 years, are remarkable in view of the low traffic density, except in the neighbourhood of Oslo, and the very extensive undeveloped areas of mountain and virgin forest."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "afad74d3-f7f2-4dec-b649-f8783b8dc689",
                                                "sense_id": "acb5668c-1d1d-3b1b-9284-332537f9454b",
                                                "text": "Camden motive power depot has been much criticised for its emission of smoke in a residential neighbourhood and its complete dieselisation is rapidly taking place."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "35ad8f00-b812-4955-b812-a61db5d0bf8b",
                                                "sense_id": "acb5668c-1d1d-3b1b-9284-332537f9454b",
                                                "text": "Another key event was the spontaneous mobilization of the Tiantongyuan neighbourhood in greater Beijing in 2008, which was an effort to modify the route plan of line no.5 of the Beijing subway system so that the neighbourhood could be more conveniently connected."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
